{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Those [A]heartaches now are on their [D]way
What [E]makes you want to be that [A]way
You [A]cheated on me and you [D]lied
[E]You put teardrops in my [A]eyes
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[E]I found out what they say is [A]true
I [B]hope someday that you'll be [E]blue
And [A]then you'll know dear why I [D]cry
[E]With these teardrops in my [A]eyes
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I heard the rumors all around
That someday you'd let me down
I turned my head and gossip flies
Cause it puts teardrops in my eyes
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I never thought you'd let me down
But now at last I understand
You've wrecked my life and broke our vow
You'll have to pay for it somehow
{end_of_chorus}
